    <item>
      <title>Don't Give Up on Peace in the Democratic Republic of Congo</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-10-16/don-t-give-up-on-peace-in-the-democratic-republic-of-congo</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">c79ac266ec99cefee8b3d7b8</guid>
      <pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 03:30:07 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>The peace deal agreed in December by the presidents of the Democratic Republic of Congo and Rwanda, brokered by a beaming President Donald Trump, was doomed to fail. The main belligerent in the conflict, the March 23 Movement (M23) rebel group that controls the mineral-rich eastern DRC, wasn’t a signatory. And the optics were inauspicious: Trump mispronounced the names of Rwanda’s Paul Kagame and the DRC’s Felix Tshisekedi, and the pair avoided eye contact and wouldn’t shake hands.</description>
      <dc:creator>Justice Malala</dc:creator>
